#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""OGFinder session script  (generated by ds9 "Analysis > Save Session as Python Script...")

Re-runs the computational steps recorded in an OGFinder (customised SAOImageDS9) GUI
session from the shell.  Python 3 standard library only; the OGFinder python steps
(sep/astropy/numpy/...) are run through --python.

  --mode pipeline  (default)  automatic steps only; use it on NEW data.  Steps that were
                              done by hand in the GUI (hand-drawn mask regions, hand-picked
                              merges/deletions, undo/redo, imported masks ...) are skipped
                              and listed; automatic substitutes are used where they exist
                              (ICL centre = brightest catalogue source, PSF stars = the
                              automatic star finder selection).
  --mode replay               every recorded step, with the recorded literal values:
                              reproduces the GUI session on the ORIGINAL inputs.

Examples
  # one image
  session.py image.fits --outdir out
  # several bands of one field
  session.py --bands F105W=a.fits F125W=b.fits F160W=c.fits --detection-band F160W --outdir out
  # many fields, 4 in parallel, resumable
  session.py --input-list fields.txt --jobs 4 --resume --outdir out
  # exact replay of the GUI session on the original files
  session.py --mode replay --outdir out F105W=... (see --help)

Outputs per field: <outdir>/<field>/{work,outputs,manifest.json,catalog_final.tsv,session.log};
combined <outdir>/summary.tsv and summary.json.
"""
